the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    Gesamtbewertung holds for *a case*.
    Modul 1 holds for *a case*; open textured.
    Modul 2 holds for *a case*; open textured.
    Gesamtbewertung is decided for *a case*.
    Gesamtbewertung would hold for *a case*; unknown.
    Modul 1 is decided for *a case*; scenario element.
    Modul 2 is decided for *a case*; scenario element.

the knowledge base r3_6_accept_delegated_custom_combiner includes:

the text of the_rulemap is at "sources/accept-delegated-custom-combiner.ruml".

% Status des ersten Kindes
Gesamtbewertung holds for a case if
    Gesamtbewertung is decided for the case
    and Modul 1 holds for the case.

Gesamtbewertung holds for a case if
    it is not the case that Gesamtbewertung is decided for the case
    and Gesamtbewertung would hold for the case.

Gesamtbewertung is decided for a case if
    Modul 1 is decided for the case
    and Modul 2 is decided for the case.

scenario generated_1 is, as stated in "accept-delegated-custom-combiner.ruml" at generated_1:
    % no data
    node_1 expects answers ["Gesamtbewertung holds for case 1"] and any unknowns.
    not_node_1 expects answers ["it is not the case that Gesamtbewertung holds for case 1"] and any unknowns.
    node_2 expects answers ["Modul 1 holds for case 1"] and any unknowns.
    not_node_2 expects answers ["it is not the case that Modul 1 holds for case 1"] and any unknowns.
    node_3 expects answers ["Modul 2 holds for case 1"] and any unknowns.
    not_node_3 expects answers ["it is not the case that Modul 2 holds for case 1"] and any unknowns.

query node_1 is:
    Gesamtbewertung holds for case 1.

query not_node_1 is:
    it is not the case that Gesamtbewertung holds for case 1.

query node_2 is:
    Modul 1 holds for case 1.

query not_node_2 is:
    it is not the case that Modul 1 holds for case 1.

query node_3 is:
    Modul 2 holds for case 1.

query not_node_3 is:
    it is not the case that Modul 2 holds for case 1.

